// LAINFLAGS: --engine=ir-full
// THE MIDPOINT IDENTITY. `a + (b - a) / D` with D >= 1 and `a <= b` lies in [a, b]: the
// quotient is non-negative and no greater than `b - a`. Both operands are values of the type,
// so the result is too and the add cannot overflow.
//
// The operand intervals refuse it — `lo` and `hi` are unbounded usize and their sum leaves u64
// — and the octagon cannot reach it either: the step needs `q + a <= b`, a bound on a SUM by a
// third VALUE, and octagons hold `x + y <= c` only for a constant c. Reading the add's own
// recorded relation instead would be circular, since that relation is recorded assuming no
// wrap, which is the thing being proven. So it is decided from wrap-free facts at check time.
//
// midpoint_identity_fail.ln pins the guard: without `lo < hi` the subtraction itself can
// underflow and nothing holds.
func mid(lo usize, hi usize) usize {
    if lo < hi { return lo + (hi - lo) / 2 }
    return lo
}
func main() i32 {
    if mid(2, 8) == 5 { return 0 }
    return 1
}
